- How would this change if edges could have negative weights? How to handle ties in reconstruction?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with bitwise operations, commonly encountered in optimization scenarios for data processing and segmentation tasks.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP formulation
- Subarray OR precomputation
- Boundary reconstruction
- Time/space complexity analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOrPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const OR = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));

  // Precompute OR for all subarrays
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let cur = 0;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      cur |= A[j];
      OR[i][j+1] = cur;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        if (dp[j][t-1] !== -Infinity) {
          const val = dp[j][t-1] + OR[j][i];
          if (val > dp[i][t]) {
            dp[i][t] = val;
            par[i][t] = j;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct blocks
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = par[curr][t];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr-1]);
    curr = start;
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity
Time: O(n²k) due to triple nested loops, Space: O(nk + n²) for DP tables and OR precomputation.

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a DP variant transforming flips into max-sum of k disjoint subarrays on a simple gain array.

## Key Concepts
- DP with two matrices: dp for best total, best for segments ending at i
- Transform 0/1 to +1/-1 gains to linearize gains
- Reconstructing segments via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesAfterKFlips(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const gain = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=> s[i]==='0'?1:-1);
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const best = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      best[i][t] = Math.max(best[i-1][t] + gain[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + gain[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], best[i][t]);
    }
  }
  const ones = s.split('').filter(c=>c==='1').length;
  return ones + dp[n][k];
}
```

